        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The phrase, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਫਿਰ ਮਿਲਾਂਗੇ = ਫਿਰ (phir, \"again\") + ਮਿਲਾਂਗੇ (milāṁge, \"we will meet\") — \"we'll meet again.\" Chapter 1 gave you ਸਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਕਾਲ (sat srī akāl), the Sikh greeting that doubles as a formal goodbye; phir milāṁge is the everyday, hopeful one — the same \"promise of return\" the whole subcontinent prefers to a blunt farewell (Hindi phir milenge, Bengali āshi, Tamil pōy varugiṟēṉ). Even more casual: phir mildē hāṁ (\"(we) meet again,\" present for a near future)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
